How to do a Pull Request:-
-Clone your repository
-Then cd into the Cloned directory
-Then create a new branch or run git checkout -b NewBranchName
- Then open the file and make changes
-Then Stage your changes
-Then git add
-Then git commit
-Then git status
-Then git push origin CurrentBranchName
-Then go to GitHub
-Click on Compare
-Now for the Compare changes Click on Branch margining into Branch you made your changes in
- Add a tittle
-Add the description of the changes
-Then Create pull request
-Now ask someone in your team to review the changes
-After it has been reviewed, you can merge it into the desired branch by clicking on Merge pull request



Main things to take note of in PR:
1.	Write small pull requests. This leaves less room to introduce bugs and provides a clearer history of changes
2.	Review your own pull requests first. Review, build, test your PR before submitting
3.	Provide context ang guidance. Write clear titles and descriptions so reviewers can quickly understand what the pull request does.


